  "_comment": "The palette-swap leitmotif one level up: the SAME rigged form-skeleton as knight-forms-rig, re-materialised as an obsidian-and-ember boss and showing off the new `diamond` form. The armour bones are `obsidian` instead of iron/steel; the surcoat and greatsword are `ember` (a glowing forge ramp). The crown gem and chest forge-heart are `ember` `diamond`s, the two pauldron spikes are `gold` `diamond`s \u2014 the new flat-faceted primitive shown in two materials, a cut gem that catches the light on one facet, unmistakably NOT a smooth sphere. Nothing about the pose was re-authored; the skeleton still meets by construction, so `connected`/`on_canvas` hold for the boss exactly as for the base knight.",
